{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"OESA-2026-4957","published":"2026-11-19T01:43:28Z","modified":"2026-11-19T02:00:11.322727192Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-16762"],"summary":"qt5-qtbase security update","details":"This package provides base tools, such as string, xml, and network handling.\r\n\r\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\nAn attacker able to supply a crafted XML document to an application using QXmlStreamReader can cause disproportionate CPU consumption during parsing, making the application unresponsive (denial of service). Exploitation requires only that the application parse attacker-influenced XML; no authentication, privileges, or user interaction beyond ingesting the input are needed. There is no loss of confidentiality or integrity — no data disclosure, data modification, or code execution — and the impact is contained to the affected process.(CVE-2026-16762)","affected":[{"package":{"name":"qt5-qtbase","ecosystem":"openEuler:24.03-LTS-SP4","purl":"pkg:rpm/openEuler/qt5-qtbase&distro=openEuler-24.03-LTS-SP4"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"5.15.10-20.oe2403sp4"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"aarch64":["qt5-qtbase-5.15.10-20.oe2403sp4.aarch64.rpm","qt5-qtbase-debuginfo-5.15.10-20.oe2403sp4.aarch64.rpm","qt5-qtbase-debugsource-5.15.10-20.oe2403sp4.aarch64.rpm","qt5-qtbase-devel-5.15.10-20.oe2403sp4.aarch64.rpm","qt5-qtbase-examples-5.15.10-20.oe2403sp4.aarch64.rpm","qt5-qtbase-gui-5.15.10-20.oe2403sp4.aarch64.rpm","qt5-qtbase-mysql-5.15.10-20.oe2403sp4.aarch64.rpm","qt5-qtbase-odbc-5.15.10-20.oe2403sp4.aarch64.rpm","qt5-qtbase-postgresql-5.15.10-20.oe2403sp4.aarch64.rpm","qt5-qtbase-private-devel-5.15.10-20.oe2403sp4.aarch64.rpm","qt5-qtbase-static-5.15.10-20.oe2403sp4.aarch64.rpm"],"noarch":["qt5-qtbase-common-5.15.10-20.oe2403sp4.noarch.rpm"],"src":["qt5-qtbase-5.15.10-20.oe2403sp4.src.rpm"],"x86_64":["qt5-qtbase-5.15.10-20.oe2403sp4.x86_64.rpm","qt5-qtbase-debuginfo-5.15.10-20.oe2403sp4.x86_64.rpm","qt5-qtbase-debugsource-5.15.10-20.oe2